  "notes": [
    "The deep gallery keeps approximately 11 m width and 5.5 m centre headroom up to the back chamber. Existing measured source relief is expanded without moving the accepted mouth or replacing the cave with primitive geometry.",
    "Only the final 1.2 m rounds into a broad rear wall; the long tapered dead end is removed. The source boundary vertices remain shared across the wall, floor and ceiling joins.",
    "The measured aisle is 54.91 m, 2.11 times the original 26.00 m. The original outdoor campfire, river, mountain mesh and castle path are unchanged.",
    "White calcite wall albedo retains real rock relief, pores and bedding; pigments are projected directly onto those existing triangles. Warm fire illuminates the same faintly visible paintings.",
    "Gallery r30 restores the user-reference waving gray-white Rimo cat among two horses, an aurochs and a deer, directly opposite the unchanged west-wall 524. The cave geometry, walking surface and fire are unchanged.",
    "Gallery r31 includes all 13 released mascots among animal friezes. Cave placement is at ground level at the mountain foot near camp. Coming Soon is reserved for confirmed upcoming characters. The source cave GLB and earlier pigment files are retained.",
    "Gallery r32 integrates the faithful small 524 with a mammoth, two horses and an aurochs in one weathered transparent frieze, matching the opposite Rimo frieze. It replaces three separated west-wall placements. Earlier paintings and source models remain archived.",
    "Gallery r33 adds Maruimo among a bison, horse and deer. All 14 released mascots are represented; the Coming Soon reserve and original GLB remain unchanged."
  ],
